    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "My relationship with math is practical, not deeply passionate. I use it in everyday life—budgeting, cooking, and even interpreting graphs in the news. I didn’t have a love-hate relationship with it in school, mostly because it didn't connect to real-world applications. It’s a tool, not a subject I’m obsessed with.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I’ve never had an anxiety attack about math. If I’m stuck on a problem, I just take a break and come back to it. I’m comfortable with uncertainty and figure out things slowly. I think my low neuroticism helps. I’ll admit, I get a little frustrated, but it’s not anxiety.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a math app last year to learn about statistics. It walked me through problems step by step. I liked how it gave me explanations for every answer. It was helpful, but I still needed to think about the material to fully understand it. It felt like a supportive tutor.",
