    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "First, take the derivative of f(x), which gives you f'(x). Set f'(x) equal to zero and solve for x. These x-values are the locations of the stationary points. Then, plug those values back into the original equation to find the y-values. These are the points on the graph.",
