    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning. They can explain problems in different ways, adapt to a student’s pace, and offer practice problems. They're great for giving instant feedback. In classrooms, they could be used for tutoring and helping students explore topics beyond the standard curriculum."
